<?xml version="1.0" encoding="ISO-8859-1"?>
<OpenGeoSysProject>
<!--
  DSM provenance (CLAUDE.md sec. 12)

  *** INCOMPLETE BY DESIGN, AND SAYS SO. Every entry below reading
  *** "TODO(Vinay): UNSOURCED" is a literal for which no source in the
  *** sec. 12.1 closed list (Beacon | EPFL | Dixon 2023 | Villar | EURAD-MS |
  *** FEBEX) exists anywhere in this tree, in git history, or in the local
  *** thm-lit / Mendeley libraries. Nothing here was inferred, rounded, or
  *** borrowed from a deck that has no header of its own. Per-literal evidence
  *** with locators, and the list of attributions that were tried and refuted:
  ***   ~/.claude/projects/-Users-vinaykumar-git-ogs/
  ***       BEACON_PRJ_PROVENANCE_LEDGER_2026-08-12.md
  *** Resolution is Vinay's call: supply locators, de-register from
  *** Tests.cmake, or grant a sec. 0.2 exemption declaring this parameter set
  *** non-physical smoke placeholders.

  Benchmark family : Beacon (geometry lineage only). No BEACON specification
                     document could be located to cite; the sec. 12.1 "Beacon"
                     family cannot be written into this header until Vinay
                     supplies a WP / deliverable + table locator.
  Geometry / BC    : axisymmetric cell on beacon_1b_domain.vtu, p_ic =
                     -1e6 Pa, top_pressure 0 Pa and bottom_pressure 1e4 Pa
                     (through-flow drive), t_end = 1e3 s.
  Purpose          : micro-macro exchange PLUMBING smoke test, softer and more
                     permeable variant of 1a01 (E = 40e6 Pa, phi0 = 0.5,
                     k = 5e-16 m2). Pi-path inactive (K absent, vdW off).

  Calibration anchor:
    source         : none. This deck performs no calibration.
    dataset row    : n/a
    target sigma   : n/a
    fitted K       : none. No potential_augmentation_prefactor tag is present,
                     so K defaults to 0.0 and the augmentation branch is
                     skipped (PotentialExchange.h:259, "Setting K = 0 (default)
                     reduces exactly to the pure vdW form"). The sec. 12.1
                     Dixon/Villar anchor rule is therefore VACUOUS here, not
                     violated. The swelling_pressures literals below are inputs
                     to the macro SaturationDependentSwelling law; they are NOT
                     calibration targets and must not be read as an anchor row.

  Material parameters (source per group):
    elastic (E, nu)            : TODO(Vinay): UNSOURCED  (E = 40e6 Pa, nu = 0.2).
                                 E = 40e6 is unique to this deck in the whole
                                 Tests/Data/RichardsMechanics tree.
    porosity split phi0/phi_tr : TODO(Vinay): UNSOURCED  (0.5 / 0.4)
    intrinsic permeability     : TODO(Vinay): UNSOURCED  (5e-16 m2)
    retention macro (Sr,m,p_b) : TODO(Vinay): UNSOURCED  (0.0 / 0.5 / 5e5 Pa)
    retention micro (Sr,m,p_b) : TODO(Vinay): UNSOURCED  (0 / 0.5 / 5e6 Pa)
    swelling law (p_sw, expts) : TODO(Vinay): UNSOURCED  (1.1e7 Pa x3, 1 1 1)
    solid density rho_s        : TODO(Vinay): UNSOURCED  (2780 kg/m3).
                                 Four independent verifications refuted the
                                 "EURAD-2 MS33 spec" attribution carried by the
                                 sibling MS33 headers: that string has no
                                 locator, the named Table TH-G does not contain
                                 a solid density at all (the value appears only
                                 in spec prose, theoretical_benchmarking.tex
                                 line 102, "2.78 g/cm3"), and the beacon decks
                                 carried 2780 from the 2026-04-10 import, six
                                 weeks BEFORE that header line existed. The
                                 real transmission path is the upstream OGS
                                 deck DoubleStructureBenchmark/
                                 double_porosity_swelling_RM.prj, which has no
                                 header and is therefore a forbidden source.
                                 Adopting the line-102 locator here would be a
                                 sec. 12.4 cross-family borrow: Vinay's call.
                                 Internal incoherence to note: every beacon
                                 deck sets micro_solid_density_reference =
                                 2650 alongside solid density 2780, i.e. two
                                 grain densities 4.7 percent apart in one file.
    micro reference state      : TODO(Vinay): UNSOURCED
                                 (rho_SR_m = 2650 kg/m3, nS_ref, n_l0).
                                 TRAP recorded so it is not repeated: 2650
                                 kg/m3 is the grain density of BOOM CLAY in
                                 GRS-202. Wrong material, and GRS is not a
                                 sec. 12.1 family.
    fluid properties           : TODO(Vinay): UNSOURCED  (viscosity 1e-3 Pa s,
                                 density 1e3 kg/m3). These are rounded values,
                                 NOT the IAPWS-95 figures at 293.15 K
                                 (1.002e-3 Pa s, 998.21 kg/m3), so an IAPWS
                                 locator does not cover them.
    biot_coefficient           : TODO(Vinay): UNSOURCED  (1.0). Commit
                                 5a0792dbb0 records an incompressible-mineral
                                 ASSUMPTION, not a measurement, and is not an
                                 ancestor of this branch. A sec. 0.2 note
                                 recording the assumption is the honest fix.
    mass transfer alpha_M      : TODO(Vinay): UNSOURCED  (1e-13).
                                 Phenomenological and fabric dependent; NOT
                                 identified by a swelling-pressure calibration
                                 (fast-exchange limit). Do not invent a family.
    reference temperature      : TODO(Vinay): UNSOURCED  (293.15 K; inert in
                                 these isothermal decks).
    BC / IC magnitudes         : TODO(Vinay): UNSOURCED. Suction ICs, hydraulic
                                 Dirichlet values, sigma0 (all zero) and the
                                 zero body force are uncited. MS33's spec
                                 initial suction is 100 MPa, i.e. 100x these
                                 values, so nothing can be inherited.
    macro_porosity_floor and
    micro_water_content_floor  : 0.0 / 0.0, NUMERICAL and inert. Declared
                                 because the parser has required the pair since
                                 commit 71366ac0d3; floor 0 is byte-identical
                                 to the unfloored path (PotentialExchange.h:
                                 199-205). Approved by Vinay 2026-08-12.
    micro EOS (a, b, rho_l0)   : TODO(Vinay): UNSOURCED
    vdW base A_Hamaker         : NUMERICAL PLACEHOLDER, term switched OFF.
                                 A=1e-30 J paired with specific_surface=1.0
                                 drives the prefactor A*Sa^3/(6*pi) to order
                                 1e-19 of its physical value. Exact zero is
                                 rejected by the parser (positivity guard,
                                 PotentialExchange.h:158-171), so a minimal
                                 positive pair is the only way to disable the
                                 branch. The same quintuple appears verbatim in
                                 the DSM unit-test harness
                                 Tests/ProcessLib/RichardsMechanics/
                                 DSMMicroMacroSingleIntegrationPoint.cpp:663.
                                 NOT a material parameter; no sec. 12.1
                                 citation applies. The literature constant it
                                 stands in for is A = 2.2e-20 J (Israelachvili
                                 and Adams 1978): DO NOT write that attribution
                                 here. Needs a sec. 0.2 exemption note from
                                 Vinay recording the switch-off intent; until
                                 then the fallback reading is UNSOURCED.
    specific surface Sa        : 1.0 m2/kg, placeholder paired with A above
                                 (MX-80 is order 1e5 to 1e6 m2/kg).

  Reference VTU    : refreshed 2026-08-12 on dsm_native_maxwell_conjugate
                     @ 40551b6aad. This is a REGRESSION BASELINE at that
                     commit, not a physics claim and not a validated result.
                     The previous baseline (2026-06-02, retrievable at
                     a6dfec842c) predated the constitutive changes on this
                     branch, among them 013990e1cd (mu_lR unified on the
                     integrable Maxwell partner), aeccc1c838 and 36dfeaddcc
                     (swelling stress recast as (1-phi_M)*p_film with a sign
                     and weighting correction), dbf20d6f1a (bare-Pi OFF path
                     retired) and 6391e357a2 (marked RESIDUAL-CHANGING).

  Live deviations carried by this deck (recorded, not papered over):
    1. bishops_effective_stress uses BishopsPowerLaw(exponent=1) where the DSM
       standard since 2026-05-29 is BishopsSaturationCutoff(cutoff=1). For 1b
       this was a regression: the ancestor deck complied until 8712c6d7ee.
    2. pressure abstol = 5e-8 Pa against a 1e6 Pa suction scale, with no
       reltols. Violates the tolerance from problem scale rule.
    3. Across the five beacon decks the Hamaker constant takes three different
       values (1e-30 / 6e-20 / 5.1e-21 J); none equals the branch literature
       value 2.2e-20 J, and the 2026-05-22 sweep 0d579e8aeb that moved all 27
       other PRJs from 5.1e-21 to 2.2e-20 missed this family.
    4. The alpha_M unit is undocumented by OGS (bare copydoc); no unit is
       asserted here on purpose.
-->
    <mesh axially_symmetric="true">beacon_1b_domain.vtu</mesh>
    <geometry>beacon_1b.gml</geometry>
    <processes>
        <process>
            <name>RM</name>
            <type>RICHARDS_MECHANICS</type>
            <integration_order>2</integration_order>
            <micro_porosity>
                <mass_exchange_coefficient>1e-13</mass_exchange_coefficient>
                <nonlinear_solver><maximum_iterations>100</maximum_iterations><residuum_tolerance>1e-8</residuum_tolerance><increment_tolerance>1e-20</increment_tolerance></nonlinear_solver>
            </micro_porosity>
            <potential_exchange>
                <enabled>true</enabled>
                <pressure_tolerance>0.0</pressure_tolerance>
                <hamaker_constant>1e-30</hamaker_constant>
                <specific_surface>1.0</specific_surface>
                <micro_solid_density_reference>2650</micro_solid_density_reference>
                <micro_solid_volume_fraction_reference>0.6</micro_solid_volume_fraction_reference>
                <initial_micro_water_content>0.1</initial_micro_water_content>
                <fd_jacobian_for_exchange>false</fd_jacobian_for_exchange>
                            <!-- Floors declared inert (0.0 = no floor), preserving the
                     pre 2026-06-17 behaviour these decks were written under;
                     the parser has required both keys since commit 71366ac0d3.
                     Value approved by Vinay 2026-08-12 (CLAUDE.md sec. 1.1),
                     same inert declaration as the MS33 form (a) decks. -->
                <macro_porosity_floor>0.0</macro_porosity_floor>
                <micro_water_content_floor>0.0</micro_water_content_floor>
            </potential_exchange>
            <constitutive_relation><type>LinearElasticIsotropic</type><youngs_modulus>E</youngs_modulus><poissons_ratio>nu</poissons_ratio></constitutive_relation>
            <process_variables><pressure>pressure</pressure><displacement>displacement</displacement></process_variables>
            <secondary_variables>
                <secondary_variable name="sigma"/><secondary_variable name="swelling_stress"/><secondary_variable name="epsilon"/><secondary_variable name="velocity"/><secondary_variable name="saturation"/><secondary_variable name="porosity"/><secondary_variable name="transport_porosity"/><secondary_variable name="dry_density_solid"/><secondary_variable name="micro_saturation"/><secondary_variable name="micro_pressure"/>
            </secondary_variables>
            <specific_body_force>0 0</specific_body_force>
            <initial_stress>sigma0</initial_stress>
            <mass_lumping>true</mass_lumping>
        </process>
    </processes>
    <media>
        <medium id="0">
            <phases>
                <phase><type>AqueousLiquid</type><properties><property><name>viscosity</name><type>Constant</type><value>1e-3</value></property><property><name>density</name><type>Constant</type><value>1e3</value></property></properties></phase>
                <phase><type>Solid</type><properties><property><name>density</name><type>Constant</type><value>2780</value></property><property><name>swelling_stress_rate</name><type>SaturationDependentSwelling</type><swelling_pressures>1.1e7 1.1e7 1.1e7</swelling_pressures><exponents>1 1 1</exponents><lower_saturation_limit>0</lower_saturation_limit><upper_saturation_limit>1</upper_saturation_limit></property></properties></phase>
            </phases>
            <properties>
                <property><name>transport_porosity</name><type>TransportPorosityFromMassBalance</type><initial_porosity>phi_tr0</initial_porosity><minimal_porosity>0</minimal_porosity><maximal_porosity>1</maximal_porosity></property>
                <property><name>biot_coefficient</name><type>Constant</type><value>1.0</value></property>
                <property><name>permeability</name><type>Constant</type><value>5e-16</value></property>
                <property><name>porosity</name><type>PorosityFromMassBalance</type><initial_porosity>phi0</initial_porosity><minimal_porosity>0</minimal_porosity><maximal_porosity>1</maximal_porosity></property>
                <property><name>reference_temperature</name><type>Constant</type><value>293.15</value></property>
                <property><name>relative_permeability</name><type>Constant</type><value>1</value></property>
                <property><name>saturation</name><type>SaturationVanGenuchten</type><residual_liquid_saturation>0.0</residual_liquid_saturation><residual_gas_saturation>0</residual_gas_saturation><exponent>0.5</exponent><p_b>5e5</p_b></property>
                <property><name>saturation_micro</name><type>SaturationVanGenuchten</type><residual_liquid_saturation>0</residual_liquid_saturation><residual_gas_saturation>0</residual_gas_saturation><exponent>0.5</exponent><p_b>5e6</p_b></property>
                <property><name>bishops_effective_stress</name><type>BishopsPowerLaw</type><exponent>1</exponent></property>
            </properties>
        </medium>
    </media>
    <time_loop>
        <processes><process ref="RM"><nonlinear_solver>nonlinear_solver</nonlinear_solver><convergence_criterion><norm_type>NORM2</norm_type><type>PerComponentDeltaX</type><abstols>5e-8 1e-13 1e-13</abstols></convergence_criterion><time_discretization><type>BackwardEuler</type></time_discretization><time_stepping><type>FixedTimeStepping</type><t_initial>0.0</t_initial><t_end>1e3</t_end><timesteps><pair><repeat>20</repeat><delta_t>50</delta_t></pair></timesteps></time_stepping></process></processes>
        <output><type>VTK</type><prefix>beacon_1b_dsm_micromacro_smoke</prefix><suffix>_t_{:time}</suffix><fixed_output_times>1e3</fixed_output_times><variables><variable>pressure</variable><variable>displacement</variable><variable>saturation</variable><variable>micro_pressure</variable><variable>micro_saturation</variable><variable>swelling_stress</variable><variable>sigma</variable></variables></output>
    </time_loop>
    <parameters>
        <parameter><name>sigma0</name><type>Function</type><expression>0</expression><expression>0</expression><expression>0</expression><expression>0</expression></parameter>
        <parameter><name>E</name><type>Constant</type><value>40e6</value></parameter>
        <parameter><name>nu</name><type>Constant</type><value>0.2</value></parameter>
        <parameter><name>phi0</name><type>Constant</type><value>0.5</value></parameter>
        <parameter><name>phi_tr0</name><type>Constant</type><value>0.4</value></parameter>
        <parameter><name>displacement0</name><type>Constant</type><values>0 0</values></parameter>
        <parameter><name>pressure_ic</name><type>Constant</type><values>-1e6</values></parameter>
        <parameter><name>dirichlet0</name><type>Constant</type><value>0</value></parameter>
        <parameter><name>top_pressure</name><type>Constant</type><value>0</value></parameter>
        <parameter><name>bottom_pressure</name><type>Constant</type><value>1e4</value></parameter>
    </parameters>
    <process_variables>
        <process_variable><name>displacement</name><components>2</components><order>1</order><initial_condition>displacement0</initial_condition><boundary_conditions>
            <boundary_condition><geometrical_set>beacon_1b_geometry</geometrical_set><geometry>left</geometry><type>Dirichlet</type><component>0</component><parameter>dirichlet0</parameter></boundary_condition>
            <boundary_condition><geometrical_set>beacon_1b_geometry</geometrical_set><geometry>right</geometry><type>Dirichlet</type><component>0</component><parameter>dirichlet0</parameter></boundary_condition>
            <boundary_condition><geometrical_set>beacon_1b_geometry</geometrical_set><geometry>bottom</geometry><type>Dirichlet</type><component>1</component><parameter>dirichlet0</parameter></boundary_condition>
            <boundary_condition><geometrical_set>beacon_1b_geometry</geometrical_set><geometry>top</geometry><type>Dirichlet</type><component>1</component><parameter>dirichlet0</parameter></boundary_condition>
        </boundary_conditions></process_variable>
        <process_variable><name>pressure</name><components>1</components><order>1</order><initial_condition>pressure_ic</initial_condition><boundary_conditions>
            <boundary_condition><geometrical_set>beacon_1b_geometry</geometrical_set><geometry>top</geometry><type>Dirichlet</type><component>0</component><parameter>top_pressure</parameter></boundary_condition>
            <boundary_condition><geometrical_set>beacon_1b_geometry</geometrical_set><geometry>bottom</geometry><type>Dirichlet</type><component>0</component><parameter>bottom_pressure</parameter></boundary_condition>
        </boundary_conditions></process_variable>
    </process_variables>
    <nonlinear_solvers><nonlinear_solver><name>nonlinear_solver</name><type>Newton</type><max_iter>30</max_iter><linear_solver>general_linear_solver</linear_solver></nonlinear_solver></nonlinear_solvers>
    <linear_solvers><linear_solver><name>general_linear_solver</name><eigen><solver_type>SparseLU</solver_type><scaling>true</scaling></eigen></linear_solver></linear_solvers>
</OpenGeoSysProject>
